Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Anna McDonald  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  61 year old female with lobulated breastmass    papilloma  Fine needle aspiration revealed groups of ductal epithelium with focal atypia  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  PRESENT AT AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   SCLEROSING INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  WITH COARSE CALCIFICATIONS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS NOTE  Ductal carcinoma in situ involves a small portion of the papilloma  as well as tissue away from the papilloma  Lobular neoplasia is identified in regions involved by sclerosing adenosis  The results of immunohistochemical staining of the ductal carcinoma in situ for estrogen receptor and progesterone receptor will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast lump   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm portion of breast parenchyma which is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm white firm mass abutting the black inked margin  Within the mass  there are calcifications as well as cystically dilated spaces  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with calcifications in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and cystically dilated spaces in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 06   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 41 59PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 07   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 47 43PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Right   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 29 CLINICAL DATA  Breast carcinoma  Previous needle biopsy of right breast shows sclerosing carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SEGMENTAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   5 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SCHIRROUS TYPE  THE EXAMINED MARGINS ARE FREE OF TUMOR  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Most of the tumor is infiltrating  minor foci of intraductal carcinoma within the mass comprise less than 5 per cent  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  STROMAL FIBROSIS  CYSTS AND MILD FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a 350 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of breast and axillary tissue with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  The skin ellipse contains a 5 5cm curvilinear non healed incision  Deep to the incision is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm biopsy cavity  lined with yellow fat and red hemorrhage  Sectioning of the breast reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm poorly demarcated  irregular  firm white mass adjacent to the biopsy cavity  The mass is close to the deep margin and close to the superior medial margin  extending from one to the other  It is 1 4cm deep to the skin at 1 0cm from the medial resection margin  A photograph is taken of the extension from superior medial to deep resection margin  Laterally the tumor infiltrates fat  Throughout the mass are focal hemorrhages  Within the superior medial aspect of tumor are multiple firm white nodules  ranging in diameter from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm  The axillary tail contains multiple firm lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  AandB  skin with tumor and biopsy cavity C E  tumor with biopsy cavity and superior inked margin F I  tumor with deep resection margin J N  tumor with superomedial resection margin O  lateral tumor with infiltration fat P  medial most resection margin Q S  cross section of tumor  representative section T  representative section of lateral parenchyma  grossly uninvolved U  representative section of inferior parenchyma  grossly uninvolved V  representative section of superior parenchyma  grossly uninvolved W  representative of medial parenchyma  grossly uninvolved X Y  single lymph node Z AD  multiple lymph nodes each disected and entirely submitted  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SEGMENTAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY   report_end  , Unchecked.
