he invasive nature  The invasive carcinoma appears to be of high grade  however  the very small size may limit accurate grading  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast needle loc   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm excisional breast specimen  The surgeon orients the lateral margin with a long stitch and the superior margin with a short stitch  The long axis of the specimen is in the anterior to posterior axis  The specimen is inked as follows  superior blue  inferior black  lateral yellow  medial green  Two localization wires are in place  one of which is an area  which abuts the anterior resection margin of the specimen  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm area of gray discoloration in this area located in the anterior inferior portion of the specimen  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow tan and without nodules or masses and with areas of white fibrous tissue  The following cassettes are submitted such that the specimen is entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial sections through anterior resection margin with described lesion particularly in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Serial sectioning from anterior to posterior with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  being most posterior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is the en face posterior resection margin  The second reported lesion from the radiograph is most likely in the cassette in or near  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain fo