s with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  long stitch axillary contents  short stitch superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm skin ellipse  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm nipple  A firm  white tan REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area of discoloration surrounds the nipple  An attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail is also present  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm firm  white mass with yellow speckles and grossly extends to 1 5cm from the deep resection margin  Further sectioning of axillary tail reveals several lymph nodes  several of which are firm  white tan while others are soft pink  The lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE 2cm in greatest diameter  SECTION CODE  A C  Representative section of mass with closest deep resection margin  D F  Additional representative sections of mass  G   Representative section of mass with overlying nipple  H I  Representative sections of unremarkable breast parenchyma away from mass  J L  Axillary lymph nodes  Also received in the same container is a separate piece of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm soft  yellow piece of fat  which is sectioned to reveal unremarkable parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted in Cassette M  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Un