ctive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm breast biopsy with a needle localization wire in place and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm granular  tan pink area with yellow flecks and focal calcification corresponding to the area of microcalcifiation at the needle tip on the accompanying x ray  This lesion abuts the inked resection margin  The lesion is submitted in A through D  with remainder of breast tissue in E through H  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR IN SITU CARCINOMA  FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASION NOT LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
