Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  29 AUG 94 at 12 58 CLINICAL DATA  69 year old female with a right axillary node  measuring 3 0cm that was positive for cancer consistent with metastatic breast carcinoma at an outside hospital  Admitted for a modified radical mastectomy  Palpable right periareolar mass biopsy and frozen for second mass today      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL TISSUE RECEIVED Revised by  Shane Meehan  MD Revised on 01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 37                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY AND MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  50    MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  50    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND PAPILLOMATOSIS  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The carcinoma is multifocal  but involvement extends to 1 5cm in greatest dimension as measured on the slide section  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  The resection margins and 19 of 19 lymph nodes are free of carcinoma  No vascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  70    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  30    NOTE  The tumor is approximately 1 0cm in maximum dimension  The resection margins and 9 of 9 lymph nodes are free of carcinoma  The intraductal component is predominantly of the cribriform type  No vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   MASS    THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface with some focal firm areas measuring 0 8cm in greatest dimension  Representative section frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The remaining tissue submitted entirely in A through H  Received in three containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  Additional left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  Three lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm are submitted in cassette A  The two smaller in entirety and the largest is bisected and half is submitted in cassette A  Labeled  Left breast and axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm left breast with a skin ellipse  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm with a 0 6cm in diameter nipple  The 2 0cm incision is superior to the nipple that is 0 5cm from the superior border of the skin ellipse  8 6cm from the lateral margin of the skin ellipse and 4 5cm from the medial tip of the skin ellipse  Twelve lymph nodes were dissected fresh from the axillary tail  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to a small REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  On cross sectioning the biopsy cavity measures 3 5cm from the lateral and the superior inferior axis and 4 5cm in the lateral dimension  The anterior surface of the biopsy cavity is 1 4cm from the deep margin  1 0cm from the superior margin and 8 0cm from the inferior portion  SECTION CODE  E  medial portion of breast  medial to the biopsy cavity  F  superior margins of the biopsy cavity on the medial aspect of the breast  G J  additional margins of the cavity  K  represents a inferior margin on the biopsy cavity  L N  representative sections of normal appearing breast  O  cross sections of the nipple  Labeled  Right breast  modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm right modified radical mastectomy with an 8 0cm axillary tail  There is an REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm skin ellipse with a 7 0cm areola  There is a 4 5cm recent horizontal incision superior to the nipple  This incision is 1 0cm from the superior border of the ellipse  4 0cm from the medial aspect of the skin ellipse and ends 8 6cm from the lateral tip of the skin ellipse  On cross section deep to the incision there is a biopsy cavity that measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm with an adjacent palpable nodule measuring 1 0cm in diameter  The biopsy cavity is 1 5cm from the deep margin  6 0cm from the inferior margin  and 6 8cm from the superior margin  Six lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Lymph nodes are bisected and submitted  SECTION CODE  P Q  a segment from the medial aspect of the biopsy cavity  The sections were bisected  R S  lateral aspect of the biopsy cavity with the deep margin  T  representative section of the nipple  U V  sections lateral to the biopsy cavity with the deep margin  W  representative section of breast parenchyma  X Z  lymph nodes  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING and INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
