he posterior black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a tan white firm  irregularly defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm area subjacent to the nipple that comes closest 1 2cm to the posterior margin  3 5cm to the superior margin  and 5 0cm to the inferior margin  A discrete mass is grossly not identified  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   firm area  to closest posterior margin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   firm area under nipple  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   firm area  to closest anterior margin  The remaining parenchyma has diffuse tan white fibrous areas  representative sections of which are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A section from the subareolar area with grossly visible small ducts  up to 0 2cm   containing white  pasty material is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes are identified in axillary tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple whole lymph nodes  1 black inked and bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One potential whole lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   additional left axillary node  are multiple yellow red fragments of soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in aggregate with a multiple potential lymph nodes up to 0 5cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is submitted in toto cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   additional superficial margin  are 6 fragments of unoriented yellow red soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in aggregate which is grossly unremarkable and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Adam J Saenz M D   on REMOVED