ion are inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an area of fibrosis which measures about 8 x 2 x 4cm located beneath the lateral part of the skin  The closest distance to the fibrotic area from deep margin is 1 0cm  The rest of parenchyma appears unremarkable except for areas of fibrosis  Sections through fibrotic area reveals also a focus of fat necrosis measuring 0 6cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections submitted as follows  E  Deep margin F S  Sections from the fibrotic area  T  Section from axillary tail area  U  Representative section from area far from the lesion  V  One section from nipple  Resident  BIZHAN BANDARCHI CHAMKHALEH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 12 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  85   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  MULTIFOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INVADING LYMPHATICS AND BLOOD VESSELS  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  15    SEE NOTE   NOTE  The largest tumor diameter is 3 7cm  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 28                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISION OR BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   UNINTERPRETABLE SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistently shown very low counts  less than 3    The assay was repeated 3 times  background was consistently high suggesting that there was a delay in tissue transport  that air drying occured  or that the tissue was not sent on wet ice  If S phase information is desired  flow cytometry should be attempted  Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  10 MAY 93 at 11 09     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 46 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 117 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 36     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm irregularly shaped piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hard  firm  yellow tan mass that extends to the margin  A touch prep is made  Tissue is taken for BRDU  estrogen receptors  A block is saved frozen  Representative sections of the mass are submitted in A through G  Additional sections of breast tissue are submitted in H through J  Re