ISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm portion of breast tissue with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  deep black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior yellow  A needle localization wire and clip are in place  Serial sectioning reveals REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area  which is ill defined  rubbery  white and homogenous  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm biopsy cavity is present in this area  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm dense nodule is adjacent to the biopsy cavity  which shows focal gritty yellow granulation  This nodule abuts the anterior margin and comes to 2 0cm from the deep margin  3 0cm from the superior margin and 1 0cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted in cassettes A L  from lateral to medial  with the biopsy cavity in cassettes F G and gritty nodule in cassette I  area of clip   Resident  HEIKE VARNHOLT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION