nfavorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 32     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     NOTE  This case is re examined after a review by pathologists at the Brigham and Women s Hospital arrived at greater lymph node count  with implications for subsequent therapy  In the right axillary node dissection  a subcapsular micrometastasis is noted in a second lymph node that was missed on initial exam  In the mastectomy specimen  one rounded nodule appears to represent replacement of an intramammary node  A   another nodule may be a replaced node  but the evidence is less definite  E   Lympho  vascular invasion is present  and many areas show a prominent lymphoid response  These findings were discussed with Dr  Barbara Smith  Kevin Camphausen and Judy Garber  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 23 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm with an attached ellipse of skin including the nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Sections reveal multiple poorly circumscribed white fibrotic nodules consistent grossly with invasive carcinoma  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to up to 2 5cm  Two of the nodules are located medially extending to up to 1 0cm from the medial resection margin  One of the nodules extends to less than 0 5cm from the deep margin  Additionally there is a poorly defined fibrotic area extending from the nipple towards the lateral aspect measuring REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm abutting the deep margin  Sections through the areola region reveals multiple dilated ducts filled with yellow thick material  Sections taken as follows  Section code  A  Small nodules  one of them to deep margin   B E  Representative sections of different nodules  F  Subareolar region  G H  Poorly defined fibrotic area  to deep margin   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superficial margin over medial tumor right  are three pieces of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  entirely submitted in cassette I  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  additional superior lateral breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  serially sectioned to reveal mature adipose tissue with no focal lesions present  A representative section in J N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to up to 1 2cm in largest dimension  submitted in O T  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing a 0 4cm lymph node  entirely submitted in cassette U  Resident  ADRIANO PIRIS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  ADD  SUPER  MARGIN OVER MEDIAL TUMOR   PART C  LYMPH NODE  ADD  SUPER  LATERAL TISSUE   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  ADD  AXILLARY   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT    LOWER LESION   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT    UPPER LESION   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 23                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   LOWER LESION     THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   UPPER LESION    THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Right breast lower lesion   are 3 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 1 0cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Right breast  upper lesion   are 4 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as B  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST   LOWER LESION   CORE BIOPSY PART B  RIGHT BREAST   UPPER LESION   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
