Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Invasive breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU PRESENT IN 3 OF 6 TISSUE BLOCKS  SEE NOTE   2  THREE AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The margins of resection are free of carcinoma  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  SKIN  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5 cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the axillary tail area  On the anterior aspect  there is an oval REMOVED_DATE x 2 1 cm unremarkable portion of tan white skin  No scar is appreciated  There is a centrally located  unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6 cm nipple  There is a 2 0 cm defect on the lateral aspect which communicates with both the anterior and posterior soft tissue margins  and is located 4 5cm lateral from the portion of the unremarkable skin  On cut surface  contiguous with this defect  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0 cm cavity  consistent with a previous biopsy site  The cavity lining is smooth  glistening  fibrotic and hemorrhagic  and the cavity once again communicates with both the lateral anterior soft tissue margin and the posterior lateral soft tissue margin  The borders of the cavity are fibrotic  measuring up to 0 2cm in thickness and contains areas of fat necrosis  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan yellow to pink  lobulated and grossly unremarkable with no additional masses or lesions identified  Within the lateral aspect near the axillary tail  several possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in greatest dimension are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of exposed cavity with the exposed area in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast skin   are two irregular tan white portions of unremarkable skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The largest portion displays a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm centrally located defect  The specimen weighs REMOVED_DATE gram in aggregate  Representative sections of both portions are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  report_end  , Unchecked.
