Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 24 CLINICAL DATA  72 year old with biopsy proven breast sarcoma  Sarcoma of breast bilaterally                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  MALIGNANT SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM WITH FOCAL LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor measures REMOVED_DATE CM in greatest dimension  The histologic features are similar to that of the previous biopsy  96 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The surgical resection margins are negative for malignancy  The tumor stains strongly for vimentin in a diffuse pattern  Rare  focal cells stain for keratin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 and CAM 5 2   High molecular weight and wide spectrum keratin  as well as EMA are negative  The focal keratin staining raises the possibility of carcinosarcoma and sarcomatoid carcinoma  Electron microscopy on the keratin positive cells is being performed and a final diagnosis will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  LEFT MEDIAL MARGIN  BIOPSY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  MALIGNANT SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor measures 3 0cm in greatest dimension and is similar histologically to the left breast  The surgical resection margins are negative for malignancy  the margin designated by double knotted suture is negative for carcinoma  BREAST  RIGHT BREAST   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED EXTENDING TO INKED SURFACE  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Histologically  the carcinoma is not similar to the malignant spindle cell neoplasm  SKIN  NODULE RIGHT CHEST WALL   EXCISION  MARKED DERMAL LYMPHECTASIA  EPIDERMAL HYPERPLASIA AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL  BREAST MASS   EXCISION  MALIGNANT SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SKIN  SKIN RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL  BREAST TISSUE   EXCISION  1  FIBROFATTY TISSUE WITH FIBROSIS AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  2  SKIN WITH CICATRIX  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 44                                                                                     ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum          ELECTRON MICROSCOPY    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       RIGHT BREAST  SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM CONSISTENT WITH FIBROSARCOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The specimen for electron microscopy has been retrieved from a paraffin block  and the resulting preservation of ultrastructural detail is markedly compromised  However  the cells can be identified as fibroblasts and myofibroblasts  with dilated rough endoplasmic reticulum  RER  and focal collections of filaments as their salient features  Some of the RER has been affected by the artifactually poor preservation to mimic tonofibrils  but high magnification reveals the strutures to be RER  No desmosomes are found  Another mesenchymal feature of the neoplasm is the presence of extracellular matrix around individual cells  At least in the sample studied  no epithelial differentiation is identified  Added by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 06     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 36     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     BREAST  LEFT AND RIGHT  BILATERAL MASTECTOMIES   MALIGNANT SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM CONSISTENT WITH FIBROSARCOMA  HIGH GRADE  GRADE 2 3 3   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Histologically  the neoplasm demonstrated rare epithelial features with focal staining for keratin raising the possibility of a sarcomatoid carcinoma  Electron microscopy of these areas demonstrated fibroblastic rather than epithelial differentiation  thus supporting a diagnosis of fibrosarcoma  Dr Rosenberg has reviewed this case and agrees with the above interpretation  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is 2 450 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 14 0cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 20 0cm skin ellipse  The breast is oriented with one pin marking the medial aspect and two pins marking the superior aspect  The overlying skin ellipse contains a centrally placed 1 5cm in diameter nipple with a 2 0cm healed scar  6 0cm medial to the nipple  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm area of indurated skin with two circumscribed areas of ulceration measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and 1 0cm located 7 0cm and 8 0cm medially to the nipple  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm well circumscribed  tan  focally brown mass that extends to the medial skin and extends 6 0cm medial to the nipple to the end of the medial skin margin  The mass comes to within 0 5cm of the closest medial margin and 0 8cm to the closest deep margin  A second 2 5cm in diameter tumor nodule is located 3 5cm deep to the larger tumor and extends to within 5 0cm of the closest deep margin lateral aspect of the specimen  The remainder of the breast tissue is tan yellow and grossly unremarkable  There is a attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm segment of tan brown pectoralis muscle on the superior medial margin 3 0cm from the medial skin edge  A representative section of the medial margin is frozen as FX 2 and submitted in cassette C  SECTION CODE  A  FX 1 B  remainder of tissue in FX 1  right breast C  FX 2  left breast D  closest medial margin  left breast E  closest medial margin  left breast F  closest deep margin  left breast G  tumor with skin and medial margin  left breast H M  tumor  representative sections  left breast N  superior margin  radial  left breast O  lateral margin  radial  left breast P  inferior margin  radial  left breast Q  second tumor nodule  left breast R  closest deep margin  adjacent to second tumor nodule S  resection of unremarkable breast T  section of pectoral muscle and deep margin U  representative section of nipple V  representative skin with scar W  representative section of tumor with skin ulceration  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast long suture lateral  short stitch superior  doubled knotted suture on margin of carcinoma  is an  REMOVED_CAS