s located 1 4cm from the superior margin  1 3cm from the medial margin  1 8cm from the inferior margin  3 3cm from the lateral margin  2 8cm from the anterior tip  and 4 5cm from the posterior tip  No masses are identified  The remainder of the specimen consists of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior tip  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior tip  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue anterior to clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue immediately anterior to clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area where clip was identified  including clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibrous tissue immediately posterior to clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibroadipose tissue away from the area of fibrous tissue  from the posterior region of the specimen  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin superior   are 3 unoriented fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin inferior   are 4 unoriented fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin medial   are 2 unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin lateral   are 3 unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 13   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 10 14PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 13   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 19 23PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  809  to chromosome 17 signals  99  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 14   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 58 30PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  3  ADDITIONAL IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY RESULTS BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION  NOTE  Additional immunostains performed on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  show that the foci of carcinoma are negative for vascular markers   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    In conjunction with the morphological findings  these foci of carcinoma are favored to represent residual invasive carcinoma  Addendum  3 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 14   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 07 07PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Excision PART B  Breast  Left  Final Margin Superior   Excision PART C  Breast  Left  Final Margin Inferior   Excision PART D  Breast  Left  Final Margin Medial   Excision PART E  Breast  Left  Final Margin Lateral   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 26 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    LOW GRADE  MOSTLY ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE TUMOR  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND SEVERAL SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMAS  NOTE  There is no evidence of vascular or lymphatic invasion  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a 