Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 MAY 01 ACCESSIONED ON  31 MAY 01 at 12 12 CLINICAL DATA  56 year old with history of breast CA  invasive right breast CA                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 06 16                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  The lymph node does not contain keratin positive carcinoma cells  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 06 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node 700   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fatty fragment with a 1 2cm lymph node  which is bisected and frozen entirely as FX 1  now as A  The remainder of the specimen is submitted as J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast re excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan skin ellipse with a centrally located poorly healed scar  A short suture designates superior  medium length suture designates lateral and the long suture designates deep aspect  The superior aspect is black inked  the inferior aspect is blue inked and the deep aspect is red inked  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with adjacent fat necrosis  and the rem