n  and 1 2cm from the lateral margin  The clip is grossly identified and removed  The remaining breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial resection margin  radial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Laterally resection margin  radially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of lesion  with the area of the clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Grossly uninvolved breast parenchyma  medial to lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further representative sections of breast tissue near lesion  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of soft tissue with two probable lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm   They are submitted entirely into cassette 1 with 1 whole lymph node inked black  and the second  non inked  lymph node is bisected  They are now resubmitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two other firm areas  not submitted for frozen  are submitted in toto in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast medial margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of yellow red adipose tissue with a suture denoting the true margin  This surface is inked black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a firm  yellow  stellate lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  which abuts the margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow and hemorrhagic  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the previously mentioned lesion in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm oriented piece of fibroadipose tissue  The sutured surface is inked black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a white pink yellow fibroadipose cut surface  No masses are grossly identified  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm oriented piece of fibroadipose tissue  The new margin is inked black and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a white yellow unremarkable cut surface  The entire specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast superior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of white yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black suture denoting the true margin  This surface is inked black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal an unremarkable white yellow hemorrhagic cut surface  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast posterior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm oriented piece of white yellow fibroadipose tissue  The new margin is now inked black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal an unremarkable white yellow fibroadipose cut surface with diffuse hemorrhage  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  RARE ATYPICAL CELLS IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  MAY REPRESENT HISTIOCYTES BUT ISOLATED  TUMOR CELLS CANNOT BE EXCLUDED  AWAIT CYTOKERATIN STAINS  Gross Dictation by Joshua Kish M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Joshua Kish M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   MEDIAL SHAV