esidual foci of ductal carcinoma in situ are widely scattered in 3 of the 9 tissue blocks  In addition  a benign intraparenchymal lymph node is identified  These additional findings were discussed with Dr  Michele Gadd on REMOVED_DATE  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Sultan  REMOVE_MRN and  left sentinel lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan pink lymph node which is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Sultan  REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a black stitch designating the 12 o clock position  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm tan pink skin ellipse with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan depressed nipple located 0 7cm from the medial skin margin  There is a 2 5cm probable semicircular scar located along the medial aspect  which comes to 0 3cm of the medial skin margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm granular tan pink area  consistent with a previous biopsy site  which contains a silver metal clip  This biopsy site is located in the upper inner quadrant and is 0 9cm of the posterior margin  Also noted in the far innermost aspect of the breast tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm gray white fibrous nodule  which comes to 1 3cm of the posterior margin  Additionally  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm vaguely stellate pink to gray white mass in the mid upper breast tissue  This area is granular on cut surface and consistent with a previous biopsy site  The