Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 09 20 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  One stitch inferior margin  two stitches lateral margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION   RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  A REMOVED_DATE CM FOCUS WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  MORE THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGINS   HEALING BIOPSY SITE   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  SELIM NASSER  MD Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 18 11                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast reexcision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm tan pink skin ellipse with a central linear 5 8cm healed scar which comes to 0 5cm of the superior medial margin  A single stitch designates the inferior margin and a double stitch the lateral margin  The superficial margin is inked yellow  the deep orange  the superior black  and the inferior blue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm defect communicating with the inferior margin  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan fluid filled cyst which comes to 0 4cm of the deep margin superiorly along the lateral half the specimen  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic region arising along the lateral half of the inferior aspect defect which comes to 0 4cm of the superficial  1 0cm the deep  and 0 9cm of the superior margin  Surrounding this region are yellow orange foci consistent with fat necrosis  Finally there is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm hemorrhagic area arising in the medial half of the specimen which is consistent with previous biopsy site and comes to 0 5cm of the superficial  0 8cm of the inferior  1 0cm of the superior and deep  and 0 4cm of the medial margin  This region is also surrounded by yellow orange foci consistent with fat necrosis  The remaining cut surface is 20  tan yellow adipose and 80  dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as follows  A  Lateral margin  radially sectioned  B  Full thickness section including all margins from lateral half of the specimen  C  Cyst  D F  First hemorrhagic region to superior  inferior  superficial  and deep margins  G  Full thickness section including all margins to inferior aspect defect  G J  Second hemorrhagic area to superior  inferior  superficial  deep  and medial margins  with the medial margin radially sectioned as J  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  AQING   AHCHEAN   CHEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
