 do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  02 MAY 03 at 15 01 Proofread by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Three cytokeratin immunostained levels of the second sentinel lymph node are negative for tumor cells  Added by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  08 MAY 03 at 12 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm portion of breast tissue marked with two undesignated sutures  The long suture is assumed to represent lateral  and the short suture is assumed to represent superior  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior blue and the superior green  There is a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm ill defined firm  gritty  tan white mass  The mass is 0 2cm  0 5cm  0 6cm  0 7cm  1 3cm and 1 5cm from the posterior  anterior  lateral  inferior  superior and medial margins respectively  The remaining breast tissue is unremarkable  Representative sections to include the entire mass are submitted as follows  A  Mass to anterior  posterior and inferior margins  B  Mass to anterior and posterior margins  C  Mass to anterior and posterior margins  D  Superior and inferior margins closest to mass  E F  Unremarkable away from mass  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin medial half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow  unremarkable portion of breast tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as G J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of unremarkable tan yellow fibrofatty breast tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as K M  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel node  are several tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  There is a small amount of attached adipose tissue  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  N  2 possible whole lymph nodes  O  1 lymph node bisected  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT SENTINEL  EXCISION PART C  BREAST RIGHT FINAL SHAVED MARGIN MEDIAL CAVITY  EX PART D  BREAST RIGHT FINAL SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL CAVITY  E , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  12 MAY 94 at 15 31 CLINICAL DATA  Status post six cycles of chemotherapy for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  tumor                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3    GROSSLY REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AND EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SUPERIOR INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  NOTE  No intraductal carcinoma is identified  No perineural  lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The tumor invades subcutaneous fat to the level of the reticular dermis  The tumor is estimated to be about 40  necrotic  LYMPH NODE  AXILLARY  BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  17 MAY 94 at 14 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 94 at 14 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two parts  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of pink tan  rubbery tissue  bisected and submitted entirely in cassette A  Received is a 630 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 9 2cm skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The skin ellipse contains a 0 9cm nipple  4 8cm areola  0 8cm from the inferior skin margin and 7 5cm from the medial margin and a 4 6cm linear  well healed scar  2 0cm from the areola in the upper outer quadrant  There is a palpable REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm slightly mobile mass which is fixed to the skin  the skin overlying the mass appears normal  The subcutaneous tissue is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm lobulated to stellate  white gray mass with focal light yellow  soft focus  0 2cm from the skin surface and extending to within 0 4cm of the inked deep margin and 1 5cm from the inked superior margin  There are multiple discrete  white grey firm nodules adjacent to this mass  up to 1 0cm in diameter  The remaining tissue consists of yellow  soft  fibroadipose tissue and white pink breast parenchyma  Eleven lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail which are pink tan and firm to rubbery ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  SECTION CODE  A  Separately submitted additional axillary tissue  B D  Axillary tail lymph nodes  E G  Representative sections of the deep margin under the tumor  H  Representative section of nipple and areola  I  Representative section of scar  J  Radial section of superior margin  K  Tumor with overlying skin  L  Tumor with adjacent yellow soft area  M  Satellite nodule  N  Representative unremarkable breast parenchyma  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Mutsumi Nozue  M D  Thomas J Lynch  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST PART B  AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
